  "reason": "RNA-only scvi/multiprofile/avgpool is currently the strongest evidence (0.650 accuracy), while image-only ResNet50 remains weak even with multiprofile avgpool (0.328 accuracy). The key uncertainty is whether a stronger image representation, ViT-L, can make the image modality useful before spending budget on multimodal fusion. config_014 changes only the image encoder relative to config_011 while keeping multiprofile and avgpool fixed, so it cleanly isolates image representation. If it substantially improves image accuracy, multimodal ViT-L experiments become justified; if not, the budget should focus on RNA-only or simpler fusion, making this the most efficient next experiment."
